{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/446853-strix-d-kindred-or-the-baron-s-childer","id":446853,"title":"Strix'd Kindred or the Baron's Childer","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-17T18:48:11-07:00","id":446853,"title":"Strix'd Kindred or the Baron's Childer","content":"Baron Ornskjolf is one of the Strix mentioned in the 2nd edition chapter of them. In a sidebar at the end of his section, it mentions that the Baron has managed to sire several childer, who are strange Mekhet as a result of his being Strix. I was wondering, what kind of stuff would you assign to one of these weird Strix-made Kindred? What do you think is appropriate? A bloodline? Some kind of smaller benefit?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T19:41:16-07:00","id":446922,"title":"","content":"Under the Stories section for the Baron, the book gives you a plot seed involving one of his childer, who has developed the ability to survive unharmed in sunlight, albiet paralyzed. Small, strange abilities like that seem like what the book is going for- that said, if ever there was an excuse to create a Bloodline based on the Strix, this would be it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2984-jibkisamabi","name":"JibKisamabi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T19:44:52-07:00","id":446928,"title":"","content":"I'd say that they have a Strix bane instead of the normal Bane they get due to being Mekhet.<br /> <br /> Abjuration seems appropriate, using their Humanity in place of their (non-existent) Rank, and their Resolve instead of Resistance. It even happens to be one of the Baron's banes!<br /> <br /> Maybe their eyes have a yellowish tint, maybe their use of Obfuscate screws with shadows in a purely cosmetic way, who knows?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T21:56:25-07:00","id":447131,"title":"","content":"Just short of an actual bloodline. Take away the extra discipline, but keep the extra curse and unique special ability of a bloodline. Later on the child could develop a bloodline based on their unique abilities.<br /> <br /> Taint of Life instead of normal kindred enhanced senses. Doom Sense. One of the Doom or Host Dread Powers requiring Shadow Potency 1 or 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T06:42:34-07:00","id":449126,"title":"","content":"Make them a new bloodline. Hells, this is exactly the situation that bloodlines are meant to model! A lineage of vampires with a little something extra to their Blood. Remember - new bloodlines are much more flexible than the old ones. Not everyone has a new discipline; the very first new bloodline, the Neglatu, don't! And, even when we do get four disciplines, there's been an emphasis on using either devotions, a merit, or something else, as the main thrust of the bloodline.<br /> <br /> So, the &quot;Strix bloodline&quot; would involve a Gift that let them purchase specific strix traits as if they were devotions. Simple and straight forwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T18:02:38-07:00","id":449956,"title":"","content":"The Baron doesn't have a bloodline and the childer lack the blood potency to create one, which is why I basically said go &quot;bloodline lite&quot; then full bloodline later if desired. Neglatu are an experiment and technically aren't actually kindred, they are Neglatu. I guess the childer could become Strixpires. They seem to be meant to be a <i>little</i> off, not full blown something else like Neglatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T19:13:58-07:00","id":450024,"title":"","content":"Bloodlines aren't hardcoded to arise only when deliberately desired by Kindred at Blood Potency 6. With sufficient narrative justification, Bloodlines can manifest in a variety of conditions, both as things people make and things that happen to them. &quot;The Baron has an unusually strong bond with his host body, and can sire Kindred.&quot; definitely sounds like the kind of territory where a Bloodline can manifest. Obviously the Baron himself doesn't manifest a Bloodline, because he's <i>Strix, </i>not Kindred. His childer seem to be fertile ground for that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> I'm still fiddling with a writeup, but I'm definitely thinking the Bloodline weakness might be manifesting the eye glow when they use Disciplines, or maybe when they Frenzy. Definitely the sort of thing that can give people a false flag when they see those Kindred using disciplines. I could even imagine some Strix creating or finding some way to &quot;infect&quot; Kindred with this kind of bloodline as a way to sow that sort of chaos, though they also have an ability that can do that effect directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T21:56:10-07:00","id":450131,"title":"","content":"If you want a &quot;yellow eyes&quot; weakness then why not just have it occur under the same conditions as a Strix. It isn't much of a weakness if they aren't likely to be confused with a Strix. Considering not everyone knows about the eyes, I think it would be too limiting to have it only occur under the limited conditions you suggest. I think you need some teeth in the weakness to create the atmosphere you want.<br /> <br /> &quot;This is to say, all bloodlines were founded by Kindred of Blood Potency 6 or greater.&quot; VtR 2.0 p. 98<br /> <br /> The childer would be BP 3, or less, without diablerie, or something else strange happening. That isn't even enough to be an Avus. If you must have a complete bloodline then I would suggest you give it to the Baron. He is a Strix, but also something else now. That is what synthesis does. Strixpires, Strixwolves, Strummies, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 03-20-2015, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T08:45:15-07:00","id":450485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/446853-strix-d-kindred-or-the-baron-s-childer?p=450131#post450131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a &quot;yellow eyes&quot; weakness then why not just have it occur under the same conditions as a Strix. It isn't much of a weakness if they aren't likely to be confused with a Strix. Considering not everyone knows about the eyes, I think it would be too limiting to have it only occur under the limited conditions you suggest. I think you need some teeth in the weakness to create the atmosphere you want.<br /> <br /> &quot;This is to say, all bloodlines were founded by Kindred of Blood Potency 6 or greater.&quot; VtR 2.0 p. 98</div> </div> </div> </div>When a bloodline is <i>founded</i>, that is, deliberately. If a bloodline happens because of outside influence, that's a different situation. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/446853-strix-d-kindred-or-the-baron-s-childer?p=450131#post450131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The childer would be BP 3, or less, without diablerie, or something else strange happening. That isn't even enough to be an Avus. If you must have a complete bloodline then I would suggest you give it to the Baron. He is a Strix, but also something else now. That is what synthesis does. Strixpires, Strixwolves, Strummies, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about counting the childer as founders of the bloodline, whatever imaginary benefit that might get them. They're victims of it in the sense that they were Embraced into it. You're getting too fixated on the mechanic of the founder when the point is that those childer he Embraces are members of it, as per the rules for joining a sire's Bloodline. It's how you get the whole &quot;Morbus makes a Morbus&quot; situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T21:12:18-07:00","id":451278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/446853-strix-d-kindred-or-the-baron-s-childer?p=450485#post450485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When a bloodline is <i>founded</i>, that is, deliberately. If a bloodline happens because of outside influence, that's a different situation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not talking about counting the childer as founders of the bloodline, whatever imaginary benefit that might get them. They're victims of it in the sense that they were Embraced into it. You're getting too fixated on the mechanic of the founder when the point is that those childer he Embraces are members of it, as per the rules for joining a sire's Bloodline. It's how you get the whole &quot;Morbus makes a Morbus&quot; situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wrote a response, but decided that it is pointless. I suggest you don't ask for help when you aren't interested in it. Nobody likes to have their time wasted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T21:47:45-07:00","id":451290,"title":"","content":"I'm interested in help. Your suggestion was good. all I did was disagree with the assessment that it specifically doesn't qualify for a bloodline. We're quibbling over a point that's less interesting than pursuing the ideas already proposed, like your bloodline-lite suggestion. I don't understand why you took that to mean I'm disinterested in hearing about it, or hearing your suggestions. Thank you for everything you've said thusfar, it's been helpful to get me to refocus my thinking on what would be meaningful/useful/cool for this situation.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of other weaknesses, like in the instance of giving them a sort of bloodline-lite. What would you propose, instead of something like the glowing eyes? Maybe some kind of more proactive Beast? Or should it be something more external? I'm looking for suggestions, whether they're for a bloodline, bloodline-lite, or something else entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T21:59:52-07:00","id":451294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JibKisamabi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/446853-strix-d-kindred-or-the-baron-s-childer?p=446922#post446922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under the Stories section for the Baron, the book gives you a plot seed involving one of his childer, who has developed the ability to survive unharmed in sunlight, albiet paralyzed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can already hear the Ordo smacking it's lips to open up that Kindred if that was true.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T08:49:48-07:00","id":452733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/446853-strix-d-kindred-or-the-baron-s-childer?p=451290#post451290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm trying to think of other weaknesses, like in the instance of giving them a sort of bloodline-lite. What would you propose, instead of something like the glowing eyes? Maybe some kind of more proactive Beast? Or should it be something more external? I'm looking for suggestions, whether they're for a bloodline, bloodline-lite, or something else entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>The interesting thing about Strix is that many of their banes can potentially be shared by vampires already. Crossroads, holy symbols, hated by beasts, can only enter when invited... Strix and vampires have more in common than either species likes to admit. If you were looking to create a bloodline-like template that isn't instantly recognized as something Strix created, you could try making them a Mekhet bloodline that has an additional bane that doesn't count toward your humanity banes, and must be a bane shared by Kindred and Strix.Alternatively, you could give them a variant of the Repulsion bane (B&amp;S 109) and choose fire or sunlight; not only will fire harm them, they have great difficulty even coming near it, to mimic the Strix's banes. <br /> <br /> In terms of special abilities, if you wanted them to be a bloodline the simplest solution would be the allow them to buy certain Dread Powers that are rules compatible with vampires, say for 3 xp each, the same cost as an in-clan discipline. You could also try developing some unique powers for them based off the Strix, but that would be more work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2984-jibkisamabi","name":"JibKisamabi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T17:39:54-07:00","id":460532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/446853-strix-d-kindred-or-the-baron-s-childer?p=451290#post451290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm interested in help. Your suggestion was good. all I did was disagree with the assessment that it specifically doesn't qualify for a bloodline. We're quibbling over a point that's less interesting than pursuing the ideas already proposed, like your bloodline-lite suggestion. I don't understand why you took that to mean I'm disinterested in hearing about it, or hearing your suggestions. Thank you for everything you've said thusfar, it's been helpful to get me to refocus my thinking on what would be meaningful/useful/cool for this situation.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of other weaknesses, like in the instance of giving them a sort of bloodline-lite. What would you propose, instead of something like the glowing eyes? Maybe some kind of more proactive Beast? Or should it be something more external? I'm looking for suggestions, whether they're for a bloodline, bloodline-lite, or something else entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Strix get more banes as their SP gose up, sounds like a good place to start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}